<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ili River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ili River flows from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian-shan">Tian Shan</a> mountains into Lake Balkhash in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. Its valley provided rich pastures and was the political heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a>. The region remained central to the khanate's eastern successor states during its decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ili-river.jpg" alt="Ili River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edmon2004 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:River-ili-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
